  "term": "desipramine",
  "definition": "Desipramine is a tricyclic dibenzazepine compound that enhances neurotransmission. It mainly works by blocking the reuptake of norepinephrine at neural synapses, and it also seems to affect serotonin transport and has minor anticholinergic activity through muscarinic receptors.",
